sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-anthrobots-26> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "That wild-type cells from the trachea move over and heal neural tissue is unexpected given their normal role in the body and could not be predicted from any current molecular or tissue-level model, which suggests screening engineered tissue interactions to uncover novel cell capabilities.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tracheal cells healing neural tissue could not be predicted from current models";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Gumuskaya G, Srivastava P, Cooper BG, Lesser H, Semegran B, Garnier S, Levin M, “Motile Living Biobots Self-Construct from Adult Human Somatic Progenitor Seed Cells”, Advanced science (Weinheim, Baden-Wurttemberg, Germany) (2024), doi:10.1002/advs.202303575; section “Discussion”. Scope: Human airway epithelium-derived Anthrobots interacting with neural tissue"
}
